// Negated-polarity sibling of 0904/0916: `without ... since` with the guard
// correlating on the CURRENT request's user, where the guard var is bound
// ONLY by the guard (the anchor is a literal). Permits an Approve when the
// requesting user has made NO Transfer since a carol Transfer anchor.
//
// Discriminates the PER-BINDING negation from a value-agnostic one:
//   @0  carol Transfer  — anchor; policy scope (Approve) does not apply.
//   @10 dave Approve    — no dave Transfer in (0,1] → permit (history path,
//                         negated guard, guard-only correlation var).
//   @20 dave Transfer   — guard event for dave's binding; scope does not
//                         apply. (Writes dave's guard streak.)
//   @30 dave Approve    — dave DID transfer at @20 → deny.
//   @40 eve Approve     — dave's Transfer must NOT count against EVE's
//                         binding → permit. A value-agnostic guard (the
//                         pre-fix streak key) wrongly denies here; an
//                         over-narrowed same-step check wrongly permits @30.
//
// The compiled backend's negated read (`select_since_negated`) must key the
// guard-streak lookup by the request's user and constrain the same-step
// guard check to that binding — the deny at @30 and the permit at @40 pin
// the two directions. Interpreter is the oracle (see expected_1.out).
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Approve",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    !Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
    since within 1h
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: "carol" }
};
